To blend different audio files and create a realistic experience of a summer day using Java, you can follow these steps:

1. Import necessary libraries: You'll need the Java Audio API (JAA) to work with audio files. Add the following dependency to your `pom.xml` file if you're using Maven:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>javax.sound</groupId>
    <artifactId>javax.sound-api</artifactId>
    <version>1.10.2</version>
</dependency>
```
Or, if you're using Gradle, add this line to your `build.gradle` file:
```groovy
dependencies {
    implementation 'javax.sound:javax.sound-api:1.10.2'
}
```

2. Load and combine audio files: Use the `AudioSystem` class to load the audio files and combine them using the `Mixer` class. Here's an example:
```java
import javax.sound.sampled.*;
import java.io.File;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class SummerDayAudio {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<AudioFile> audioFiles = new ArrayList<>();
        audioFiles.add(new AudioFile("birds_chirping.wav"));
